# Gradle

- Use the Kotlin DSL only (`settings.gradle.kts` and `build.gradle.kts`).
- Apply a plugin with `alias(libs.plugins.<name>)`.
- Write each version in `gradle/libs.versions.toml`, as a range. Do not write
  a version in a build script.
- Ask the user before you add a library, a plugin or a repository. Tell the
  user that a plugin runs code at build time.
- Declare the repositories only in `settings.gradle.kts`, with
  `FAIL_ON_PROJECT_REPOS`.
- Apply the ben-manes plugin `com.github.ben-manes.versions` at the root.
- Turn on the build cache and the configuration cache in `gradle.properties`
  (`org.gradle.caching=true` and `org.gradle.configuration-cache=true`).<% if has .all "kotlin" %>
  `setup:deps:30-kotlin` runs Gradle with `--no-configuration-cache`, because
  its resolve tasks cannot use that cache.
- Without the ben-manes plugin, `mise run setup --upgrade` does not give the
  report of the old versions.
- The locking rules are in the bootstrap section of `CLAUDE.md`.<% end %>

Read `references/conventions.md` for the conventions, and
`references/local.md` for the own rules of this repository.
